# DriveBy API Validation Framework - Cursor Rules

## Project Overview
DriveBy is a thesis-ready API validation framework implementing Documentation-Driven Testing (DDT).
Monorepo structure — see CLAUDE.md for full architecture details.

## Monorepo Layout
```
driveby/
├── driveby-cli/       # Go CLI (own go.mod: github.com/meter-peter/driveby/driveby-cli)
│   ├── cmd/driveby/   # Entry point
│   └── internal/      # cli, spec, loader, engine, principles, testing, types, report, github, logger
├── apis/              # Sample APIs (perfect-api)
├── kubernetes/        # Helm chart + raw YAML examples
├── samples/           # Configs, reports, demo workflows
├── thesis/            # LaTeX thesis (7 chapters)
└── tools/             # Python/bash batch testing utilities
```

## Architecture
- Dependency flow: `types` <- `spec` <- `loader` <- `principles` <- `testing` <- `engine` <- `cli`
- `spec.APISpec` abstraction is mandatory — no raw `*openapi3.T` in validators
- Each principle (P001-P008) implements `PrincipleChecker` interface
- CLI config shared via `config.go` — no duplication

## Validation Principles (P001-P008)
- **P001**: OpenAPI Specification Compliance (critical)
- **P002**: API Documentation Quality (critical)
- **P003**: Error Handling Standards (critical)
- **P004**: Request Schema Definitions (critical)
- **P005**: Security Standards (critical)
- **P006**: API Contract Testing (critical)
- **P007**: Performance Requirements (warning)
- **P008**: API Versioning Strategy (warning)

## Build & Test
```bash
cd driveby-cli && go build ./cmd/driveby    # Build
cd driveby-cli && go test ./...              # Test
cd driveby-cli && go vet ./...               # Lint
make up                                       # Start docker-compose
make validate                                 # Run validation
```

